# Logging (Spring Boot)

## SLF4J / Logback

- Use SLF4J API; Logback via Spring Boot; configure in logback-spring.xml (or application.yml); use placeholders {} for parameters.
- Levels: ERROR, WARN, INFO, DEBUG; set level per package; LOG_LEVEL or logging.level.* in config.

## MDC (Correlation ID)

- Put correlationId (and traceId if using Sleuth/Micrometer) in MDC at filter/interceptor; clear after request.
- Include %X{correlationId} in pattern; propagate to downstream HTTP (header) and logs.

## Micrometer

- Metrics: use MeterRegistry; counters, timers, gauges; tag with key dimensions; integrate with actuator and monitoring.
- Tracing: Sleuth or Micrometer Tracing; trace ID in MDC and logs; propagate to RestClient/callers.

## Conventions

- Structured context (MDC); correlation ID on every request; no secrets in logs; appropriate level; use parameters not string concat.

## Anti-Patterns

- Logging secrets; no correlation ID; wrong level; string concatenation in log message

**See also:** `error-handling.mdc`, `controllers.mdc`
